        "uuid": "c5d246d0_548d182f",
        "filename": "zephyr/subsys/ap_pwrseq/x86_non_dsx_common_pwrseq_sm_handler.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 281,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-04T16:35:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My goal is that the AP_PWRSEQ_DRIVER option never defines `board_ap_power_force_shutdown`.  These weakly defined board functions are not a good design pattern.\n\nUsing ifdefs seems like a good approach here.  The alternate would be to declare prototypes for both ap_pwrseq_post_event() and board_ap_power_force_shutdown() that are valid for both options types.\n\n```\nvoid ap_power_force_shutdown()\n#ifdef CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ_DRIVER\n    ap_pwrseq_post_event();\n#else\n    board_ap_power_force_shutdown()\n#endif\n```",
      "parentUuid": "4df318a8_8ff9fb49",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 281,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 281,
